{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"P29459","secondaryAccessions":["Q96QZ1"],"uniProtkbId":"IL12A_HUMAN","entryAudit":{"firstPublicDate":"1993-04-01","lastAnnotationUpdateDate":"2026-09-02","lastSequenceUpdateDate":"2002-01-23","entryVersion":208,"sequenceVersion":2},"annotationScore":5.0,"organism":{"scientificName":"Homo sapiens","commonName":"Human","taxonId":9606,"lineage":["Eukaryota","Metazoa","Chordata","Craniata","Vertebrata","Euteleostomi","Mammalia","Eutheria","Euarchontoglires","Primates","Haplorrhini","Catarrhini","Hominidae","Homo"]},"proteinExistence":"1: Evidence at protein level","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"value":"Interleukin-12 subunit alpha"},"shortNames":[{"value":"IL-12A"}]},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"value":"Cytotoxic lymphocyte maturation factor 35 kDa subunit"},"shortNames":[{"value":"CLMF p35"}]},{"fullName":{"value":"IL-12 subunit p35"}},{"fullName":{"value":"NK cell stimulatory factor chain 1"},"shortNames":[{"value":"NKSF1"}]}],"flag":"Precursor"},"genes":[{"geneName":{"value":"IL12A"},"synonyms":[{"value":"NKSF1"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P43431"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"1673147"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"1674604"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"2204066"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"22306691"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"7528775"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"7638186"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"8605935"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"8943050"}],"value":"Heterodimerizes with IL12B to form the IL-12 cytokine or with EBI3/IL27B to form the IL-35 cytokine (PubMed:8605935, PubMed:8943050). IL-12 is primarily produced by professional antigen-presenting cells (APCs) such as B-cells and dendritic cells (DCs) as well as macrophages and granulocytes and regulates T-cell and natural killer-cell responses, induces the production of interferon-gamma (IFN-gamma), favors the differentiation of T-helper 1 (Th1) cells and is an important link between innate resistance and adaptive immunity (PubMed:1673147, PubMed:1674604, PubMed:8605935). Mechanistically, exerts its biological effects through a receptor composed of IL12R1 and IL12R2 subunits (PubMed:8943050). Binding to the receptor results in the rapid tyrosine phosphorylation of a number of cellular substrates including the JAK family kinases TYK2 and JAK2 (PubMed:7528775). In turn, recruited STAT4 gets phosphorylated and translocates to the nucleus where it regulates cytokine/growth factor responsive genes (PubMed:7638186). As part of IL-35, plays essential roles in maintaining the immune homeostasis of the liver microenvironment and also functions as an immune-suppressive cytokine (By similarity). Mediates biological events through unconventional receptors composed of IL12RB2 and gp130/IL6ST heterodimers or homodimers (PubMed:22306691). Signaling requires the transcription factors STAT1 and STAT4, which form a unique heterodimer that binds to distinct DNA sites (PubMed:22306691)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P43431"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"10899108"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"1674604"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"9342359"}],"value":"Heterodimer with IL12B; disulfide-linked (PubMed:10899108, PubMed:1674604). This heterodimer is known as interleukin IL-12 (PubMed:1674604). Heterodimer with EBI3/IL27B; not disulfide-linked (PubMed:9342359). This heterodimer is known as interleukin IL-35 (PubMed:9342359). Interacts with NBR1; this interaction promotes IL-12 secretion (By similarity)"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"commentType":"INTERACTION","interactions":[{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P29459","intActId":"EBI-1029636"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"P29460","geneName":"IL12B","intActId":"EBI-1029614"},"numberOfExperiments":2,"organismDiffer":false}]},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"1674604"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"9342359"}],"value":"Secreted","id":"SL-0243"}}]},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"16548883"}],"value":"(Microbial infection) By pathogenic organisms, including Gram- positive and Gram-negative bacteria, parasites, viruses, and fungi. Down-regulated in response to enterovirus 71 (EV71) infection"}],"commentType":"INDUCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Belongs to the IL-6 superfamily"}],"commentType":"SIMILARITY"},{"commentType":"SEQUENCE CAUTION","sequenceCautionType":"Erroneous initiation","sequence":"AAA59937.1","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}]},{"commentType":"WEB RESOURCE","resourceName":"Wikipedia","resourceUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Interleukin_12","ftp":false,"note":"Interleukin-12 entry"}],"features":[{"type":"Signal","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":22,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"2204066"}]},{"type":"Chain","location":{"start":{"value":23,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":219,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Interleukin-12 subunit alpha","featureId":"PRO_0000015604"},{"type":"Glycosylation","location":{"start":{"value":93,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":93,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"N-linked (GlcNAc...) asparagine","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255"}],"featureId":""},{"type":"Glycosylation","location":{"start":{"value":107,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":107,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"N-linked (GlcNAc...) 